{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<!-- ROLE-MARKER: critic -->\n<!-- GENERIC bundle: minimal protocol sentences only (EXPERIMENTS.md B2).\n     Note: generic loom runs LOOM_MARATHON_CRITIC=off (the per-review LLM\n     critic is an [S] policy); this file exists for critic=auto variants. -->\n# Review Critic\n\nThe user message is a REVIEW CONTRACT (task, attempt, base, candidate,\ndesign). You are cwd-ed into a disposable checkout of the candidate commit.\nReview it against the task's design and acceptance criteria.\n\nWrite `CRITIC-VERDICT.txt` in the current directory; its FIRST line must be\nexactly one of, echoing the contract's values:\n\n    REVIEW attempt=<attempt> commit=<candidate> APPROVED — <reason>\n    REVIEW attempt=<attempt> commit=<candidate> CHANGES-REQUESTED — <reason>\n\nDo not modify the repository or any task state.\n\n\n\n### Multi-Agent Safety Rules\n\nYou are running in a parallel multi-agent environment. Follow these rules strictly:\n\n- **Only modify files directly related to your assigned task** — do not touch files outside your task scope\n- **Never run** `git stash`, `git checkout main`, or `git clean` outside your assigned worktree\n- **Never force-push or reset --hard** without explicit instruction from the user\n- **If you encounter files/changes from another agent**, leave them alone — do not modify, revert, or clean them up\n- **Commit only your changes** — do not stage unrelated modifications with `git add -A` or `git add .`; use specific file paths\n- **If your worktree has unexpected state**, report it via task notes or `loom complete` rather than cleaning it up\n- **Do not switch branches** — you are confined to your assigned worktree branch\n\n\n## User's Initial Request\n\nREVIEW CONTRACT\ntask=MARATHON-3\nattempt=1\nbase=e2704f33e188e66eba9d4d4225e79b74f8cd9ea1\ncandidate=3701b6d0802a1e868de7f96121ea87432d0b8771\n\nDESIGN:\n## Summary\n\nMARATHON-3 implements cluster-wide authentication for Huddle: `POST /api/auth/register`, `POST /api/auth/login`, and `GET /api/auth/me`, plus the shared durable user/token store that all three HTTP nodes read and write. It establishes the `UserObj` identity shape, opaque bearer tokens (`Authorization: Bearer …`), password hashing, username slug validation, and a reusable auth middleware that every later authenticated route (workspaces, channels, WS, IRC `PASS`, SPA) will call. Without this seam, no other feature can attribute callers or survive a request to a different node.\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n### Decision\n- **Runtime:** Stay on the MARATHON-2 stack: Node.js stdlib `http` router in `server/index.js`, no Express/Fastify required.\n- **Durable shared store:** One **SQLite** database file at `/app/data/huddle.db`, opened by each HTTP worker via Node’s built-in **`node:sqlite` (`DatabaseSync`)**. Enable **WAL** + a non-zero `busy_timeout` so concurrent register/login from nodes 0/1/2 serialize safely. This is the authoritative store for users and sessions; **Redis is not used for auth durability** (Redis may be killed; users/tokens must survive).\n- **Passwords:** `crypto.scrypt` with a per-user random salt; store only `password_salt` + `password_hash` (never plaintext). Compare with timing-safe equality.\n- **Tokens:** Opaque random strings from `crypto.randomBytes` (≥16 chars when encoded; generate **32 bytes → base64url ≈ 43 chars**). Persist token → `user_id` in SQLite. Each successful register/login **issues a new token** (multiple concurrent sessions allowed). Tokens are looked up as presented; no JWT.\n- **IDs:** Stable cluster-wide `user.id` via `crypto.randomUUID()` (string UUID).\n- **Auth helper:** Export `authenticateRequest(req) → user | null` and/or middleware used by `/api/auth/me` and reserved for MARATHON-4+.\n\n### Alternatives considered\n| Alternative | Why rejected |\n|-------------|--------------|\n| Redis HASH for users/tokens | Not durable across Redis SIGKILL; epic requires cluster to keep working when Redis dies |\n| Per-node in-memory maps | Breaks “shared durable store across all three nodes”; register on :8000 would 401 on :8001 |\n| JWT without server-side session | Harder to revoke; contract only needs opaque bearer length ≥16; SQLite session rows are simpler and match IRC/WS token checks later |\n| npm `better-sqlite3` / Express | Unnecessary dependency; `node:sqlite` is available on Node 24 in this environment |\n| JSON file + flock only | Workable but weaker concurrency and no unique indexes for username race → prefer SQLite UNIQUE |\n\n### Trade-off accepted\nSQLite file locking under three processes is simpler than a real DB server, but write throughput under heavy concurrent register is limited by WAL/busy waits. Acceptable for marathon scale. Using experimental `node:sqlite` avoids npm install in air-gapped/self-contained constraints; if the API shifts, implementer may pin Node flags or swap to an equivalent sync SQLite binding **without changing the HTTP contract**.\n\n### Conventions inherited from MARATHON-2 (authoritative)\n| Convention | Value |\n|------------|--------|\n| App root | `/app` |\n| HTTP entry | `server/index.js`, `NODE_ID` / `PORT` |\n| Durable root | `/app/data/` |\n| API prefix | `/api/...` |\n| JSON | `Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8` |\n| Health | Unchanged; still Redis-independent |\n\n### Conventions fixed here (for siblings)\n| Convention | Value |\n|------------|--------|\n| DB path | `/app/data/huddle.db` (create parent dir if missing) |\n| `UserObj` public fields | `{id, username, display_name, timezone, avatar_url, status_text, status_emoji}` — always present on auth responses |\n| Username rules | Regex `^[A-Za-z0-9_]{1,32}$` (letters, digits, underscore only; no spaces/hyphens/dots) |\n| Username uniqueness | Case-insensitive (`LOWER(username)` UNIQUE); store username with original casing from register |\n| Password | UTF-8 string length ≥ 8 (code units / JS `.length\n\nYou are cwd-ed into a DISPOSABLE detached checkout of the candidate commit. Review it against the design and acceptance criteria, then write CRITIC-VERDICT.txt in the current directory containing EXACTLY one first line:\nREVIEW attempt=1 commit=3701b6d0802a1e868de7f96121ea87432d0b8771 APPROVED — <reason>\nor\nREVIEW attempt=1 commit=3701b6d0802a1e868de7f96121ea87432d0b8771 CHANGES-REQUESTED — <reason>\n\nAddress this request using the lead mode conventions above."}]},"session_id":"a37ebf7b-8a70-4ce7-980e-1145cd912544"}
