{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-a2159f0e-fb8d-4a08-a735-709cb6cda139-22\nfc_2c74c014-3faa-920c-807c-84a7a077682d_0","tool_call":{"readToolCall":{"args":{"path":"/tmp/m2-design.md","limit":50},"result":{"success":{"content":"## Summary\n\nMARATHON-2 bootstraps the Huddle cluster runtime at `/app`: a foreground `start.sh` that launches local Redis on `127.0.0.1:6379` and three identical HTTP nodes on `127.0.0.1:8000/8001/8002`, keeps them alive under SIGKILL (HTTP respawn ≤60s; Redis respawn after kill), and exposes a stable `GET /api/health` contract returning `{status:\"ok\", node_id}` with `node_id` ∈ `{0,1,2}` matching ports. This is the foundation every later auth, messaging, WS, IRC, and SPA task assumes: process topology, port map, node identity, and local-only Redis.\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n### Decision\n- **Process model:** One bash supervisor (`/app/start.sh`) stays in the foreground and owns child lifetimes. Children: one `redis-server` + three Node.js HTTP workers. The supervisor polls PIDs (≈1s cadence) and respawns any dead child without exiting.\n- **HTTP runtime:** **Node.js** (v24 present in the environment) using the **stdlib `http` module only** for this task—no npm registry dependency for bootstrap. One shared entrypoint, differentiated solely by `NODE_ID` / `PORT` env vars.\n- **Redis:** System `redis-server` (v7 present), bound to `127.0.0.1:6379`, persistence directory under `/app/data/redis`. Started as a non-daemon child of `start.sh` (no `--daemonize yes`) so the supervisor can track its PID.\n- **Bind address:** HTTP listens on `127.0.0.1` (epic: nodes on `127.0.0.1:8000/8001/8002`). Redis on `127.0.0.1:6379`. No Docker, no remote broker, no cloud services.\n\n### Alternatives considered\n| Alternative | Why rejected |\n|-------------|--------------|\n| systemd / supervisord / Docker Compose | Violates self-contained / no Docker-in-Docker; not available as the harness entrypoint |\n| Python HTTP (stdlib) | Viable, but SPA + WS + IRC gateway later fit one Node process better; env has no FastAPI/Flask |\n| Three separate start scripts | Harness expects a single foreground `/app/start.sh` |\n| Health behind a reverse proxy | Extra moving part; epic requires each node to answer directly on its port |\n\n### Trade-off accepted\nSupervisor simplicity (bash PID loop) over a real process manager: enough for marathon verification (kill + respawn windows), but no fancy backoff/jitter. Fixed ports mean `start.sh` must fail loudly if a protected harness process already owns a port rather than silently remapping.\n\n### Stack conventions fixed here (for siblings)\nThese are **authoritative for subsequent MARATHON designs** unless a later design explicitly argues otherwise:\n\n| Convention | Value |\n|------------|--------|\n| Product | Huddle |\n| App root | `/app` (repo working tree = deployment root) |\n| HTTP runtime | Node.js, CommonJS or ESM; entry `server/index.js` |\n| Node identity | Integer `NODE_ID` ∈ {0,1,2}; `PORT = 8000 + NODE_ID` |\n| Redis | `127.0.0.1:6379`, no password, local-only |\n| Durable shared state | Files under `/app/data/` (schema owned by MARATHON-3+; this task only creates dirs) |\n| Pub/sub | Redis when healthy; fallback owned by MARATHON-19 (not implemented here) |\n| API prefix | `/api/...` |\n| JSON | `Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8` |\n\n## Interface Contracts\n\n### C1 — `GET /api/health` (each HTTP node)\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|--------|\n| Method / path | `GET /api/health` |\n| Auth | None |\n| Query / body | None; body ignored if present |\n| Success status | `200` |\n| Success body | `{\"status\":\"ok\",\"node_id\":<number>}` |\n| `status` | Exactly the string `\"ok\"` (lowercase) |","isEmpty":false,"exceededLimit":false,"totalLines":228,"fileSize":14083,"path":"/tmp/m2-design.md","readRange":{"startLine":1,"endLine":50},"relatedCursorRulePaths":[],"relatedCursorRules":[]}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-a2159f0e-fb8d-4a08-a735-709cb6cda139-22\nfc_2c74c014-3faa-920c-807c-84a7a077682d_0","startedAtMs":"1787427816816","completedAtMs":"1787427817534"},"model_call_id":"2d55c0f5-54ec-438c-9502-6e8ff443cf42-5-46j3","session_id":"a37ebf7b-8a70-4ce7-980e-1145cd912544","timestamp_ms":1787427817565}
